{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And it shall be a witness</b> — the Holy One, blessed be He; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 31:44). But it is not according to its plain sense. Rather, he says: and the covenant shall be a witness between us, for whoever violates it shall be cursed with all the imprecations of the covenant, in the manner of \"and they shall be in you for a sign and for a wonder\" (Deuteronomy 28:46). Or its meaning is: a covenant was struck in an enduring thing that would be a witness between us; therefore Jacob set up a stone, and this is what he said: \"this heap is a witness, and the pillar is a witness,\" in the manner of \"and Joshua said, this stone shall be a witness among us\" (Joshua 24:27)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:01.368797478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}